# send-email

Send email through the LBV Gmail account using the configured app password.

## Usage

```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/send-email.js '<json>'
```

## Parameters (JSON object)

| Field | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `to` | yes | Recipient email address |
| `subject` | yes | Email subject line |
| `body` | yes | Plain text body |
| `cc` | no | CC address |
| `bcc` | no | BCC address |

## Examples

Send a welcome email:
```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/send-email.js '{"to":"customer@example.com","subject":"Your LBV order is confirmed","body":"Hi, your order is confirmed. We will follow up within 24 hours."}'
```

Send with CC:
```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/send-email.js '{"to":"customer@example.com","cc":"andrey@birthoflight.org","subject":"Blueprint delivered","body":"Your Blueprint is ready. Download link: ..."}'
```

## Output

Success: `{"ok":true,"messageId":"<id>","to":"...","subject":"..."}`
Failure: `{"ok":false,"error":"..."}`

## Rules

- Always construct the `body` as plain text — no HTML
- From address is always the LBV Gmail account — do not change
- Double-check `to` address before sending — this sends real email
- Never send bulk or marketing email through this tool; use it for transactional/operational messages only
- If `ok` is false, report the error to Apex and do not retry without investigation
